 "says": "Alice binds her device key and registers the package candidate the target will run: its runtime module (workenv/contracts/c03.py), an asset (the cutover plan schema) and a shipped check (compose/check-domains.py), each copied from source_commit, and provenance.json made at pack time. She then submits one cutover plan to the target: one explicit transfer of the data she selected, whose quiesced capture names the source revision and outbox captured after the old writers stopped and the import validated against exactly them; all three owners sealed with nothing in flight; the entrance trace verified with no writer left unrouted; one commit; the old source kept; and candidate_digest naming the candidate just registered. The owner commits the cutover once. What must not happen: ownership moving before the verified stage, the cutover installing any package other than the registered candidate, or the old source being deleted.",
 "spec_sha256": "862c4c511ff02bc33a3f09bfc8487b983a318c96cc761efe6fb215c721fe3ed1",
 "steps": [
  {
   "carries": [
